{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They shall pour out</b> — And the king, if he was good, every man will pour forth his goodness, and it says <b>the abundance of Your goodness</b>. And the meaning is: Your abundant goodness, like <b>the greatness of Your arm</b> (Exodus 15:16), which is Your great arm." "<b>And Your righteousness they shall exult</b> — It is also fitting that the king act justly." "And the word <b>they shall exult</b> — in public. And this they say — <b>Gracious</b> — to save one who cries out to Him. <b>And merciful</b> — to guard His servant lest he stumble."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {0 "Resolved the verse quotation to Exodus 15:16 based on the phrase בגדול זרועך.", 2 "The bracketed text in the source appears to be a parenthetical gloss on subsequent words in the psalm (חנון ורחום)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:51.252750272Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}